00:38:58.766 --> 00:39:01.633
You put some kind
of air intake in the mask.


00:39:01.669 --> 00:39:03.637
Boy, you better...
now I'm assuming


00:39:03.671 --> 00:39:06.367
that the material is
see-through, right?


00:39:06.407 --> 00:39:08.739
Yeah, dude, I'ma tell you something.
Rick, this is good.


00:39:08.776 --> 00:39:12.007
I'm impressed.
Like really impressed.


00:39:22.990 --> 00:39:25.550
Hey, that's my spot.


00:39:25.593 --> 00:39:28.061
You're sitting on my gargoyle.
Move it.


00:39:28.095 --> 00:39:30.723
- Excuse me?
- What are you even doing here?


00:39:30.765 --> 00:39:32.858
I'm looking seriously
out over the city


00:39:32.900 --> 00:39:35.801
in a squatting position.


00:39:35.837 --> 00:39:37.828
Well, that's what I do here.
So if you're not moving,


00:39:37.872 --> 00:39:40.067
I guess we're gonna
have to share.


00:39:40.107 --> 00:39:41.267
Uh, okay, fine.


00:39:41.309 --> 00:39:43.869
I actually usually
perch in the front.


00:39:43.911 --> 00:39:46.471
Oh, all right.
Well, here, you've got to go around.


00:39:46.514 --> 00:39:49.039
- Okay, wait.
- Just turn this way. Here we go.


00:39:49.083 --> 00:39:51.051
- Dude!
- You're right, I'm sorry. Relax.


00:39:51.085 --> 00:39:52.746
- Okay okay.
- Okay okay.


00:39:55.456 --> 00:39:58.050
- Uh, I can't perch like this.
- God, me neither.


00:39:58.092 --> 00:40:00.151
- What's your name?
- John Storm.


00:40:00.194 --> 00:40:02.662
Dragonfly.
So what's your power?


00:40:02.697 --> 00:40:05.063
What's my power?
Stand back.


00:40:07.034 --> 00:40:10.060
- Flame on!
- Whoa!


00:40:10.104 --> 00:40:12.368
Huh?


00:40:12.406 --> 00:40:15.273
I'm on fire!


00:40:15.309 --> 00:40:17.709
Get a blanket or something!
Holy shit!


00:40:17.745 --> 00:40:21.181
It's not working!
Get the fire extinguisher!


00:40:23.351 --> 00:40:24.613
Ah! No! Ah!


00:40:24.652 --> 00:40:26.916
God! You idiot, stop!


00:40:26.954 --> 00:40:28.922
What's wrong with you?


00:40:38.833 --> 00:40:41.097
Sorry, my bad.


00:40:45.940 --> 00:40:50.138
Rick, once you understand
the true nature of heroism,


00:40:50.177 --> 00:40:52.145
you will fly.


00:40:55.182 --> 00:40:57.980
Shit.


00:41:16.837 --> 00:41:21.171
This Dragonfly,
he's not even a hero.


00:41:21.208 --> 00:41:24.336
He's not... I have... I have...
I have just a... I have...


00:41:25.713 --> 00:41:28.682
He can't...
he can't even fly.


00:41:30.418 --> 00:41:32.409
The Dragonfly
can't even fly!


00:41:35.990 --> 00:41:38.458
I can fly, okay?


00:41:39.460 --> 00:41:41.394
I can fly.


00:41:41.429 --> 00:41:43.090
This just in:


00:41:43.130 --> 00:41:45.724
Tom Cruise is dead.


00:41:45.766 --> 00:41:48.234
World's most powerful man.


00:41:49.637 --> 00:41:52.333
I have a feeling you might
disagree with that.


00:41:55.209 --> 00:41:57.643
Strom, do you have
my test results?


00:41:57.678 --> 00:42:00.146
Yes, sir.


00:42:02.917 --> 00:42:06.785
Whatever you're doing
to your... victims,


00:42:06.821 --> 00:42:09.949
rejuvenates you.
But only for 24 hours.


00:42:09.991 --> 00:42:11.788
Hmmm.


00:42:11.826 --> 00:42:15.318
What if I killed 28 people
in one session?


00:42:15.363 --> 00:42:17.331
Would that give me
a month to live?


00:42:17.365 --> 00:42:19.697
If it were February, yes.


00:42:19.734 --> 00:42:21.361
But only if your cells
could absorb


00:42:21.402 --> 00:42:23.734
that much energy at once,
and they can't.


00:42:23.771 --> 00:42:26.831
I'm afraid
you have to kill each day


00:42:26.874 --> 00:42:28.808
to live each day.


00:42:28.843 --> 00:42:31.505
Still a slave
to the tyranny of time.


00:42:31.545 --> 00:42:33.877
There must be some answer.


00:42:33.914 --> 00:42:35.882
There isn't.


00:42:35.916 --> 00:42:38.510
Unless...


00:42:38.552 --> 00:42:41.988
unless you had
some cerillium.


00:42:42.023 --> 00:42:44.651
Then you could create
a device powerful enough


00:42:44.692 --> 00:42:47.252
to draw the life-force out
of thousands of people


00:42:47.294 --> 00:42:49.558
and enhance your own
cellular capacity.


00:42:49.597 --> 00:42:52.031
Strom, you're a genius.


00:42:52.066 --> 00:42:54.762
Wikipedia.
But that's not important.


00:42:54.802 --> 00:42:58.329
What is important is that you
don't have any cerillium.


00:42:58.372 --> 00:43:00.602
Besides, it's immoral.
We don't do that sort of thing.


00:43:00.641 --> 00:43:02.233
We're a pharmaceutical
company.


00:43:02.276 --> 00:43:04.608
Wait a minute.


00:43:06.013 --> 00:43:08.106
Take a look.


00:43:08.149 --> 00:43:09.912
Hawking's lab is
in the physics building.


00:43:09.950 --> 00:43:11.315
I could just
walk right in.


00:43:11.352 --> 00:43:14.719
You're going
to steal cerillium?


00:43:14.755 --> 00:43:18.213
No, not me.


00:43:18.259 --> 00:43:19.920
I'm a law abiding citizen.


00:43:19.960 --> 00:43:22.258
But perhaps there's
someone inside me.


00:43:22.296 --> 00:43:25.424
Someone unfettered
by the rule of law.


00:43:25.466 --> 00:43:30.267
Someone who will,
at any cost, survive!


00:43:30.304 --> 00:43:32.568
Ow!


00:43:32.606 --> 00:43:34.904
Oh, glass in my eye.
Glass in my eye!


00:43:34.942 --> 00:43:37.968
- Does it hurt?
- Uh, yeah, it hurts.


00:43:38.012 --> 00:43:41.539
Well, if you could spread...
spread them with your fingers.


00:43:41.582 --> 00:43:43.550
Push your lids
with your fingers.


00:43:43.584 --> 00:43:45.449
- Two... two... two fingers.
- Are your fingers clean?


00:43:45.486 --> 00:43:47.647
That's it. And roll
your eyeball around.


00:43:47.688 --> 00:43:49.417
- And push it.
- I'm rolling it!


00:43:49.457 --> 00:43:51.755
Dig it out with
another piece of glass.


00:43:51.792 --> 00:43:53.487
Are you fricking insane?


00:43:53.527 --> 00:43:55.552
I'll get the tweezers.


00:43:57.198 --> 00:43:59.496
Read about the Dragonfly,
world's greatest hero.


00:43:59.533 --> 00:44:01.160
- Right here?
- Right here, yup.


00:44:01.202 --> 00:44:02.692
Read all about it.


00:44:14.348 --> 00:44:16.646
No, you listen to me!


00:44:16.684 --> 00:44:19.312
I want that story
on my desk or you're fired!


00:44:19.353 --> 00:44:20.513
Who the hell are you?


00:44:20.554 --> 00:44:22.613
I was wondering if you've
got a job opening for...


00:44:22.656 --> 00:44:26.023
Job?! How dare you come in here
and ask me for a job?


00:44:26.060 --> 00:44:29.029
I'm the editor in chief!
I know the mayor of Venus!


00:44:29.063 --> 00:44:31.258
Hamburgers can see
the future!


00:44:31.298 --> 00:44:32.822
- Rosie O'Donnell...
- Sorry about this.


00:44:32.867 --> 00:44:34.801
We share the building
with a mental hospital.


00:44:34.835 --> 00:44:37.736
Bad news, boss. We're nowhere on
those Dragonfly photos.


00:44:37.772 --> 00:44:40.036
Damn. Those were
tomorrow's lead.


00:44:40.074 --> 00:44:42.201
What about these?


00:44:45.513 --> 00:44:49.847
Wow! it's almost like
you're the Dragonfly.


00:44:49.884 --> 00:44:51.511
Uh, no no no.
See?


00:44:51.552 --> 00:44:53.986
Look.


00:44:54.021 --> 00:44:55.921
Now that's photography.


00:44:55.956 --> 00:44:58.652
Just heard on the scanner, some kind
of police standoff at Empire University.


00:44:58.692 --> 00:45:01.627
We'll need photos.
Kid, I want you to...


00:45:01.662 --> 00:45:03.596
Where'd he go?


00:45:09.570 --> 00:45:11.902
Come on, let's go!


00:45:18.779 --> 00:45:21.748
This is the chief of police.
We have the building surrounded.


00:45:21.782 --> 00:45:23.477
Come out with your hands up.


00:45:26.687 --> 00:45:29.087
What the hell is that?


00:45:42.536 --> 00:45:45.300
I am the Hourglass.


00:45:45.339 --> 00:45:48.365
And your time is up.


00:45:58.352 --> 00:46:00.217
Get him, Dragonfly.


00:46:07.695 --> 00:46:09.720
It's over, Hourglass.


00:46:09.763 --> 00:46:12.425
No, Dragonfly.


00:46:22.309 --> 00:46:25.176
It's just begun!


00:46:26.780 --> 00:46:29.271
It's useless to resist.


00:46:29.316 --> 00:46:31.181
I'll fight you
to my last breath.


00:46:31.218 --> 00:46:35.086
Like the sands of time
I am unceasing and relentless.


00:46:35.122 --> 00:46:37.022
Evil never triumphs,
Hourglass.


00:46:37.057 --> 00:46:39.958
You'll pay for your crimes
and justice will...


00:46:39.994 --> 00:46:42.121
stop!
Stop!


00:46:42.162 --> 00:46:44.153
Stop!


00:46:44.198 --> 00:46:46.496
Are you okay?


00:46:46.533 --> 00:46:49.661
No.


00:46:53.507 --> 00:46:55.441
Titanium blades.


00:46:55.476 --> 00:46:57.171
They cut through diamonds.


00:46:57.211 --> 00:46:59.702
I'm not wearing any diamonds.


00:47:02.549 --> 00:47:04.210
Ooh, ow!


00:47:05.319 --> 00:47:07.549
Ow!


00:47:07.588 --> 00:47:10.751
I wish I could stay longer,
Dragonfly.


00:47:10.791 --> 00:47:14.124
But I just don't
have the time.


00:47:19.967 --> 00:47:23.733
Whoever this Dragonfly is,
he's in over his head.


00:47:23.771 --> 00:47:25.932
We don't need so-called
superheroes.


00:47:25.973 --> 00:47:28.203
What Empire City needs
is more cops.


00:47:28.242 --> 00:47:30.142
And a Hooters.


00:47:32.179 --> 00:47:35.615
Titanium blades. Looks like someone
found your weakness.


00:47:35.649 --> 00:47:37.173
It's not my weakness.


00:47:37.217 --> 00:47:40.448
I'm sorry, I forgot.
Your weakness is you can't fly.


00:47:40.487 --> 00:47:41.852
Maybe if you had a partner.


00:47:41.889 --> 00:47:43.151
I don't need help.


00:47:46.961 --> 00:47:50.158
I'm fine all by myself.


00:47:50.197 --> 00:47:52.097
She means a lot to you,
doesn't she?


00:47:52.132 --> 00:47:54.396
What?
Oh, no.


00:47:54.435 --> 00:47:57.029
I mean, she's with
someone else.


00:47:57.071 --> 00:47:58.834
Well, maybe
that's for the best.


00:47:58.872 --> 00:48:00.669
After all,
it could be dangerous,


00:48:00.708 --> 00:48:03.142
you know, being the girlfriend
of the Dragonfly.


00:48:03.177 --> 00:48:05.202
I don't know what
to do, Aunt Lucille.


00:48:05.245 --> 00:48:07.236
- I love her.
- So be it.


00:48:07.281 --> 00:48:09.181
But remember,
to get to you


00:48:09.216 --> 00:48:12.879
your enemies will attack
the people you care for the most.


00:48:12.920 --> 00:48:16.720
Be careful not to hurt
the ones you love.


00:48:18.359 --> 00:48:20.293
And shave your pubes.


00:48:20.327 --> 00:48:22.852
No one wants to go down
on a tumbleweed.


00:48:33.674 --> 00:48:35.539
Jill!


00:48:35.576 --> 00:48:36.975
Rick?


00:48:37.011 --> 00:48:39.138
I heard you were auditioning
for a part so...


00:48:39.179 --> 00:48:41.147
Oh, they're beautiful.


00:48:41.181 --> 00:48:43.445
God, you are so supportive.


00:48:43.484 --> 00:48:46.453
Why can't Lance
be more like you?


00:48:48.555 --> 00:48:51.149
There's something you're not
telling me, isn't there?


00:48:51.191 --> 00:48:52.590
Something secret.


00:48:52.626 --> 00:48:55.390
Something locked away
deep inside.


00:48:55.429 --> 00:48:57.590
It was summer camp.
We had to share a shower.


00:48:57.631 --> 00:48:59.724
You trip and fall with your mouth
open on one guys...


00:48:59.767 --> 00:49:01.394
No!


00:49:01.435 --> 00:49:04.871
I mean, in here.


00:49:07.741 --> 00:49:10.835
Well, there is...


00:49:12.379 --> 00:49:15.143
Keep your identity a secret, Rick.


00:49:17.418 --> 00:49:20.444
Dude, you're like a real superhero, man!


00:49:20.487 --> 00:49:23.820
Once a month
you'll bleed from you vagina.


00:49:26.894 --> 00:49:28.623
I...


00:49:28.662 --> 00:49:30.789
nothing.


00:49:32.332 --> 00:49:35.233
Nothing?


00:49:38.472 --> 00:49:40.269
Well, I should go.


00:49:41.442 --> 00:49:43.910
You're a good friend.


00:49:46.980 --> 00:49:47.081
Hey, check this out.


00:49:47.081 --> 00:49:50.209
Hey, check this out.


00:49:50.250 --> 00:49:52.115
Oh, shit.


00:49:54.088 --> 00:49:56.181
- Let's go.
- Get her.


00:50:37.764 --> 00:50:40.028
Oh God, it hurts.
It hurts.


00:50:40.067 --> 00:50:42.661
Please stop!
I'm begging you!


00:50:56.850 --> 00:50:59.478
Wait!


00:51:01.155 --> 00:51:04.147
- Where are you?
- Behind you.


00:51:06.426 --> 00:51:08.451
You saved my life.


00:51:08.495 --> 00:51:10.861
Do I get to thank you?


00:51:53.874 --> 00:51:56.138
Go.
Be a hero.


00:52:13.460 --> 00:52:15.189
Yeah.


00:52:25.405 --> 00:52:27.396
It looks like you're planning
a mass murder.


00:52:27.441 --> 00:52:29.306
Would you like help?


00:52:29.343 --> 00:52:30.935
Paper clip guy.


00:52:47.160 --> 00:52:50.459
I'm so happy that you
and your boyfriend


00:52:50.497 --> 00:52:52.488
are spending Thanksgiving
with us.


00:52:52.532 --> 00:52:54.466
Of course, Lucille.


00:52:54.501 --> 00:52:56.401
You need support
at a time like this.


00:52:56.436 --> 00:52:59.963
Yes, I miss seeing
my Albert each morning.


00:53:00.007 --> 00:53:02.339
You know, 50 years
of marriage


00:53:02.376 --> 00:53:04.310
creates quite a bond.


00:53:04.344 --> 00:53:06.141
I wish I knew love
like that.


00:53:06.179 --> 00:53:07.908
Oh, you will, dear.


00:53:07.948 --> 00:53:10.644
You just have to
follow your heart.


00:53:10.684 --> 00:53:13.448
That's the thing.
I don't know if I can.


00:53:13.487 --> 00:53:15.182
Oh, Jill.


00:53:15.222 --> 00:53:18.749
If you can't trust yourself
who can you trust?


00:53:18.792 --> 00:53:20.521
I know.


00:53:20.560 --> 00:53:22.551
But what if my heart
is telling me to be with someone


00:53:22.596 --> 00:53:23.961
I can't be with?


00:53:23.997 --> 00:53:25.760
It's not just any guy.
It's the...


00:53:25.799 --> 00:53:28.097
forget it.
You'll think I'm crazy.


00:53:28.135 --> 00:53:29.693
No, of course not.


00:53:29.736 --> 00:53:31.704
You can tell me anything.


00:53:31.738 --> 00:53:33.797
I'm very good
at keeping secrets.


00:53:33.840 --> 00:53:36.434
You'll think it's
ridiculous, but...


00:53:36.476 --> 00:53:38.808
it's the Drag...


00:53:38.845 --> 00:53:40.369
- I'll get it.
- Thank you.


00:53:42.616 --> 00:53:45.551
Hey, babe.


00:53:45.585 --> 00:53:48.782
Oh, I forgot to tell you
I kinda invited my uncle.


00:53:48.822 --> 00:53:52.087
- Your uncle?
- What? Set another plate.


00:53:52.125 --> 00:53:54.025
Well, okay.
I guess.


00:53:54.061 --> 00:53:57.519
Miss Johnson. Please,
excuse my nephew's poor manners.


00:53:57.564 --> 00:54:00.590
- Thank you.
- Mrs. Adams, I'm Lou Landers.


00:54:00.634 --> 00:54:02.659
I hope this isn't
too much of an imposition.


00:54:02.703 --> 00:54:05.570
Oh, of course not.
There's always room for one more.


00:54:05.605 --> 00:54:06.902
Thank you.


00:54:06.940 --> 00:54:09.033
It's just Thanksgiving
is for family.


00:54:09.076 --> 00:54:11.010
Lance is the only family
I have.


00:54:11.044 --> 00:54:12.978
- I never married.
- Fruitcake?


00:54:13.013 --> 00:54:15.345
Nope, just never met
the right woman.


00:54:15.382 --> 00:54:19.216
Ah, yes, Lance told me
Rick Riker was your neighbor.


00:54:19.252 --> 00:54:20.947
Where is Rick?


00:54:23.690 --> 00:54:26.250
That's odd.


00:54:26.293 --> 00:54:29.387
I thought he was out.
I'll go check on him.


00:54:29.429 --> 00:54:32.057
Please, you're busy.
Allow me.


00:54:32.099 --> 00:54:34.624
Thank you.
Upstairs, second door to the right.


00:54:51.685 --> 00:54:53.516
Rick?


00:55:04.331 --> 00:55:06.128
Hmmm.


00:55:15.075 --> 00:55:16.406
Hmmm.


00:56:33.153 --> 00:56:35.883
Sorry I'm late.


00:56:35.922 --> 00:56:38.755
Oh, Mr. Landers.


00:56:38.792 --> 00:56:40.589
Rick.


00:56:40.627 --> 00:56:42.561
No, you're just on time.


00:56:42.596 --> 00:56:44.791
Everybody,
take your seat.


00:56:44.831 --> 00:56:46.355
Ohhh.


00:56:46.399 --> 00:56:49.368
Ah ah ah!
Not till we say grace.


00:56:49.402 --> 00:56:51.165
Jesus!


00:56:51.204 --> 00:56:52.603
Amen.


00:56:54.207 --> 00:56:55.834
Please start,
everyone.


00:56:55.876 --> 00:56:57.810
This all looks
so delicious, Lucille.


00:56:57.844 --> 00:57:00.745
We have Rick
to thank for it.


00:57:00.780 --> 00:57:03.374
Ever since Albert...


00:57:03.416 --> 00:57:06.579
Rick has been supporting me
with his new job.


00:57:06.620 --> 00:57:08.884
New job?
You didn't tell me.


00:57:08.922 --> 00:57:12.915
Oh well, I'm sort of the Dragonfly's
unofficial photographer.


00:57:16.229 --> 00:57:17.856
What happened to your arm?


00:57:19.599 --> 00:57:21.499
Uh...


00:57:21.535 --> 00:57:24.026
a bike messenger
knocked me down.


00:57:25.272 --> 00:57:27.399
I see
your wrist is bandaged.


00:57:27.440 --> 00:57:30.409
Yes, I burned it
on some hot coffee.


00:57:30.443 --> 00:57:32.411
And you have a cut on your lip.


00:57:32.445 --> 00:57:34.379
Uh...


00:57:34.414 --> 00:57:37.110
my crackpipe broke.


00:57:38.585 --> 00:57:40.985
You have a scratch
on your neck.


00:57:41.021 --> 00:57:43.421
Yes, I...


00:57:43.456 --> 00:57:46.254
met a girl
on Craigslist.


00:57:46.293 --> 00:57:48.352
And you have a bruise
on your neck.


00:57:48.395 --> 00:57:50.329
I...


00:57:50.363 --> 00:57:52.661
met a guy
on Craigslist.


00:57:55.435 --> 00:57:57.960
I'm sorry, Lance.
We have to go.


00:57:58.004 --> 00:58:00.495
- Why?
- I...


00:58:00.540 --> 00:58:02.531
shat my pants.


00:58:03.977 --> 00:58:05.842
I'll drive.


00:58:19.759 --> 00:58:22.319
- Thanks for helping clean up.
- Of course.


00:58:22.362 --> 00:58:25.058
Poor thing's so tired.


00:58:25.098 --> 00:58:27.760
Yeah, well, you know
old folks after a big meal.


00:58:27.801 --> 00:58:30.736
So... you know the Dragonfly?


00:58:30.770 --> 00:58:32.533
Uh...


00:58:32.572 --> 00:58:34.233
yeah, I guess.


00:58:34.274 --> 00:58:36.538
You could sorta say
we're close.


00:58:36.576 --> 00:58:39.943
Has he...
has he ever asked about me?


00:58:39.980 --> 00:58:41.971
Um, yeah.


00:58:42.015 --> 00:58:44.483
- Yeah, once.
- What did you tell him?


00:58:45.986 --> 00:58:47.851
Well, I said...


00:58:47.887 --> 00:58:48.979
I told him...


00:58:50.056 --> 00:58:52.923
I told him, "The thing
about Jill is...


00:58:52.959 --> 00:58:56.417
when you look in her eyes
and she looks back in yours...


00:59:00.967 --> 00:59:02.662
- you know that
you'd do anything


00:59:02.702 --> 00:59:05.330
anything to be a better person
than you are.


00:59:05.372 --> 00:59:06.964
So that...


00:59:08.375 --> 00:59:11.401
- if you were ever
lucky enough to be with her,


00:59:11.444 --> 00:59:14.470
you could earn every second
of her perfect...


00:59:21.354 --> 00:59:24.448
- grace,
and her limitless beauty...


00:59:29.496 --> 00:59:31.487
- and her unending love.


00:59:33.833 --> 00:59:35.323
- Don't cry.
- I'm not.


00:59:35.368 --> 00:59:37.268
My eyes are burning.


00:59:39.139 --> 00:59:40.868
Rick, I want you to know


00:59:40.907 --> 00:59:42.898
that was the most
beautiful thing


00:59:42.942 --> 00:59:44.773
anyone's ever said to me.


00:59:50.417 --> 00:59:53.011
- Scented candle?
- Thank you.


00:59:54.421 --> 00:59:57.879
Rick, I'm so confused, and yet...


00:59:59.426 --> 01:00:01.758
- I know exactly
what I want.


01:00:21.047 --> 01:00:23.777
Sorry to drop in uninvited.


01:00:23.817 --> 01:00:26.980
It's okay. We were hoping someone
would open a window.


01:00:27.020 --> 01:00:29.488
It was getting stuffy
in here.


01:00:29.522 --> 01:00:33.049
So this is the lair
of the Dragonfly.


01:00:33.093 --> 01:00:35.994
- How did you...
- No no no,


01:00:36.029 --> 01:00:40.398
I'm not here to fight you. I've got
thousands of other people I plan to kill.


01:00:40.433 --> 01:00:43.664
This little visit
is just to show you


01:00:43.703 --> 01:00:47.230
who'll get hurt
if you get in my way.


01:00:47.273 --> 01:00:49.241
Never!


01:01:00.620 --> 01:01:03.919
Time to go.


01:01:09.529 --> 01:01:12.020
The woman, Lucille Adams
of East Empire City,


01:01:12.065 --> 01:01:14.465
- was badly injured.
- How was she injured?


01:01:14.501 --> 01:01:16.332
- Badly.
- What about the Dragonfly?


01:01:16.369 --> 01:01:18.360
All I can tell you is this:


01:01:18.404 --> 01:01:20.668
he didn't save
anyone tonight.


01:01:20.707 --> 01:01:23.141
Doctor, how is she?


01:01:23.176 --> 01:01:25.610
I'm afraid your aunt's
taken a turn for the worse.


01:01:25.645 --> 01:01:28.739
She can't speak, she can't walk,
she had no control over her bowels.


01:01:28.782 --> 01:01:30.147
That's... that's awful.


01:01:30.183 --> 01:01:32.674
I know. I went ahead and set up
a MySpace page for her


01:01:32.719 --> 01:01:35.279
under "crazy shit machine."


01:01:35.321 --> 01:01:36.948
She already has 40 friends.


01:01:36.990 --> 01:01:39.288
Wait a minute.
That's somebody else's aunt.


01:01:39.325 --> 01:01:41.589
Your aunt has no problem
with her bowels...


01:01:41.628 --> 01:01:43.562
- Oh, thank God.
...because she's dead.


01:01:43.596 --> 01:01:46.759
I'm truly sorry, Rick,
but there is a silver lining.


01:01:46.800 --> 01:01:49.132
Your uncle came out
of his coma this morning.


01:01:49.169 --> 01:01:50.397
He did?


01:01:50.436 --> 01:01:53.428
Yes, but you mustn't tell him about
your aunt just yet.


01:01:53.473 --> 01:01:56.442
He's in a delicate mental state.
The slightest bit of bad news


01:01:56.476 --> 01:01:59.104
could send him spiraling
right back into a coma.


01:01:59.145 --> 01:02:00.942
I understand.


01:02:03.116 --> 01:02:05.516
Mr. Adams,
you have a visitor.


01:02:05.552 --> 01:02:08.612
- Is it Lucille?
- No, sir, it's not your dead wife.


01:02:08.655 --> 01:02:10.452
It's your nephew Rick.


01:02:10.490 --> 01:02:12.685
Remember, no bad news.


01:02:12.725 --> 01:02:15.592
Now, sir, here you go.
This is my bill.


01:02:15.628 --> 01:02:19.120
- You did surgery on me?
- Yes, sir, we confused you


01:02:19.165 --> 01:02:21.030
with one of our
sex-change patients,


01:02:21.067 --> 01:02:23.365
but don't worry,
we didn't remove your penis.


01:02:23.403 --> 01:02:26.338
We did cut your testicles off, but, well,
since your wife's dead,


01:02:26.372 --> 01:02:27.964
you won't be
needing them anyway.


01:02:28.007 --> 01:02:29.804
You just want
to keep his spirits up.


01:02:29.843 --> 01:02:31.970
He'll land on his feet
in no time.


01:02:33.546 --> 01:02:36.709
We are gathered today to say goodbye


01:02:36.749 --> 01:02:39.616
- to Lucille Adams.
- Goodbye!


01:02:39.652 --> 01:02:42.314
And now the eulogy.


01:02:42.355 --> 01:02:44.721
It's tragic to think this is the last time


01:02:44.757 --> 01:02:47.225
that I can look
upon my wife's face.


01:02:47.260 --> 01:02:49.490
God, Lucille!


01:02:49.529 --> 01:02:53.829
How could you take her from me?
I can't live without her!


01:02:53.867 --> 01:02:55.801
Ahhh!


01:02:55.835 --> 01:02:58.201
Lucille!
Snookie lumps!


01:02:58.238 --> 01:03:00.206
I'm sorry, there's been
a terrible mistake.


01:03:00.240 --> 01:03:03.107
- This is your wife.
- Ah!


01:03:03.142 --> 01:03:05.303
She is this man's wife.


01:03:07.647 --> 01:03:10.548
Give me five minutes.


01:03:14.420 --> 01:03:16.285
- Uncle Albert!
- I'm not finished.


01:03:21.027 --> 01:03:23.257
You're one lucky guy.
Now...


01:03:23.296 --> 01:03:24.786
where's Lucille?


01:03:24.831 --> 01:03:27.925
Ah, Lucille!


01:03:34.407 --> 01:03:37.342
I do have this coupon
for a cremation.


01:03:41.781 --> 01:03:43.339
Rick?


01:03:44.684 --> 01:03:47.175
I am so sorry
for your loss.


01:03:49.422 --> 01:03:51.447
What is it?


01:03:51.491 --> 01:03:53.618
I know I said some things,


01:03:53.660 --> 01:03:55.651
but now more than ever,
I realize...


01:03:57.063 --> 01:03:58.997
we can never be together.


01:03:59.032 --> 01:04:01.762
I don't believe you.


01:04:03.536 --> 01:04:06.937
You love me, Rick.
I know you do.


01:04:06.973 --> 01:04:10.374
Jill, trust me.
I'm telling you this for your own good.


01:04:14.280 --> 01:04:16.111
I don't love you.


01:04:18.151 --> 01:04:20.142
You're no longer
in my five.


01:04:21.721 --> 01:04:23.689
How could you?


01:04:29.762 --> 01:04:31.491
# When I was young #


01:04:32.765 --> 01:04:36.166
# I never needed anyone #


01:04:38.604 --> 01:04:42.335
# Makin' love
was just for fun #


01:04:44.010 --> 01:04:46.808
# Those days are gone #


01:04:53.886 --> 01:04:59.984
# All by myself #


01:05:00.026 --> 01:05:02.654
# Don't wanna be #


01:05:02.695 --> 01:05:07.564
# All by myself #


01:05:07.600 --> 01:05:09.431
# Anymore #


01:05:10.603 --> 01:05:15.905
# All by myself #


01:05:17.310 --> 01:05:18.800
# Don't wanna be #


01:05:18.845 --> 01:05:23.578
# All by myself. #


01:05:23.616 --> 01:05:27.108
# Anymore #


01:05:27.153 --> 01:05:32.853
# All by myself #


01:05:32.892 --> 01:05:35.019
# Don't want to be #


01:05:35.061 --> 01:05:39.521
# All by myself #


01:05:39.565 --> 01:05:42.864
# Anymore #


01:05:42.902 --> 01:05:47.362
# All by myself. #


01:05:53.079 --> 01:05:54.910
You can't keep
getting lucky, man.


01:05:54.947 --> 01:05:57.177
You only beat me
by two strokes this time.


01:05:57.216 --> 01:05:59.616
And the back nine
is what killed.


01:05:59.652 --> 01:06:01.449
Oh my God!


01:06:01.487 --> 01:06:04.285
- Look at this place.
- Yo, what are you doing, man?


01:06:04.323 --> 01:06:06.484
You gotta pull
yourself together, dude.


01:06:06.526 --> 01:06:09.893
What's the point?


01:06:14.100 --> 01:06:16.125
Look at you...
eating junk food,


01:06:16.169 --> 01:06:19.764
wearing fake beards,


01:06:19.806 --> 01:06:22.934
and we found your costume
in the garbage outside.


01:06:22.975 --> 01:06:25.466
Yeah, well, I'm not
the Dragonfly anymore.


01:06:25.511 --> 01:06:28.344
But you said the Hourglass
was going to kill thousands of people.


01:06:28.381 --> 01:06:31.578
I told you I'm no hero.
All right? Aunt Lucille's dead,


01:06:31.617 --> 01:06:33.448
I've rejected the only girl
I've ever loved


01:06:33.486 --> 01:06:35.784
and I can't even fly.


01:06:37.256 --> 01:06:40.589
I wish I'd never been bitten
by that stupid dragonfly.


01:06:40.626 --> 01:06:43.823
And maybe your father
shouldn't have given you this after all.


01:06:43.863 --> 01:06:47.492
Look at the words
your ancestors inscribed in that ring.


01:06:47.533 --> 01:06:50.730
"Honor, valor, sacrifice,


01:06:50.770 --> 01:06:53.170
duty, commitment,
bravery, justice,


01:06:53.206 --> 01:06:55.003
integrity, brotherhood,


01:06:55.041 --> 01:06:58.169
self-esteem, low prices,
affordable housing,


01:06:58.211 --> 01:07:00.873
loose-fitting pants,
cheap internet porn."


01:07:01.881 --> 01:07:03.872
The rest is in Latin.


01:07:03.916 --> 01:07:06.180
Rick, the hero's path
is dangerous.


01:07:06.219 --> 01:07:09.916
You may fail or you may fly.
All that matters


01:07:09.956 --> 01:07:13.119
is that you do it
for the best of reasons.


01:07:13.159 --> 01:07:15.150
Helping others, Rick,


01:07:15.194 --> 01:07:17.560
that's what makes you
a real hero.


01:07:19.232 --> 01:07:21.063
Maybe you're right,


01:07:21.100 --> 01:07:23.534
but even if I wanted to stop
the Hourglass,


01:07:23.569 --> 01:07:25.434
I wouldn't know
where to start.


01:07:25.471 --> 01:07:28.235
I mean, where's he gonna
find thousands of people in one place?


01:07:28.274 --> 01:07:30.765
Look.


01:07:30.810 --> 01:07:33.643
Reporting here live from the
Empire City convention center


01:07:33.679 --> 01:07:36.113
where thousands of people
are in one place,


01:07:36.149 --> 01:07:38.242
but none of them
more important


01:07:38.284 --> 01:07:40.684
than the attendees
of the World Humanity Awards.


01:07:40.720 --> 01:07:43.154
I'll drive.


01:07:45.625 --> 01:07:49.755
Well, that shortcut through the playground
sure saved us some time.


01:07:49.795 --> 01:07:51.956
You go ahead,


01:07:51.998 --> 01:07:54.262
I'll find
a place to park.


01:07:56.302 --> 01:07:58.634
Mister, please stop!


01:07:58.671 --> 01:08:01.139
Each year
the World Humanity Awards


01:08:01.174 --> 01:08:03.438
are held to honor
the greatest achievements


01:08:03.476 --> 01:08:05.740
on behalf of all humanity.


01:08:05.778 --> 01:08:07.803
This gala event
is expected to draw


01:08:07.847 --> 01:08:10.543
the world's most prestigious
leaders to Empire City.


01:08:10.583 --> 01:08:12.813
- Excuse us, excuse us!
- "Empire City Times."


01:08:12.852 --> 01:08:16.083
Damn! Look,
there go Prince Charles.


01:08:16.122 --> 01:08:18.147
And Nelson Mandela.
Nelson!


01:08:18.191 --> 01:08:20.022
Hey, I was
in jail too, man.


01:08:21.894 --> 01:08:24.419
One of the guests here
is the Hourglass.


01:08:24.463 --> 01:08:26.328
But which one?


01:08:27.967 --> 01:08:30.231
Thank you so much
for inviting us, Mr. Landers.


01:08:30.269 --> 01:08:32.464
Well, when you're being
honored by the world,


01:08:32.505 --> 01:08:34.063
you want
your family with you.


01:08:35.741 --> 01:08:39.177
Perhaps one day, you could
be part of our family too.


01:08:40.513 --> 01:08:43.243
Ladies and gentlemen,
our first award


01:08:43.282 --> 01:08:46.046
is for the medical
breakthrough of the year.


01:08:46.085 --> 01:08:48.280
For his company's
pioneering work


01:08:48.321 --> 01:08:50.789
in the field
of feminine hygiene


01:08:50.823 --> 01:08:53.690
I award Lou Landers
douchebag of the year.


01:08:55.394 --> 01:08:57.954
# Douchebag #


01:08:57.997 --> 01:09:00.966
# He's the douchebag
of the year #


01:09:01.000 --> 01:09:03.560
# Now ain't
he great, folks? #


01:09:03.603 --> 01:09:06.731
# Ain't he grand?
The douchebag of the year. #


01:09:12.378 --> 01:09:15.370
# Douchebag #


01:09:15.414 --> 01:09:18.850
# He's Mr. Douchebag
of the year #


01:09:18.884 --> 01:09:21.478
# Look at him smile,
look at him shine #


01:09:21.520 --> 01:09:25.149
# He's the douchebag of,
the douchebag of the year. #


01:09:25.191 --> 01:09:28.752
Hold up the douchebag!
Hold up the douchebag, sir.


01:09:31.364 --> 01:09:33.628
Stop right there, Landers.


01:09:33.666 --> 01:09:36.100
Mr. Riker.
So...


01:09:36.135 --> 01:09:37.602
you know.


01:09:37.637 --> 01:09:39.798
You're damn right I do.


01:09:41.207 --> 01:09:43.505
Someone in this auditorium
is the Hourglass.


01:09:43.542 --> 01:09:46.602
I need your help
to figure out who it is.


01:09:46.646 --> 01:09:48.773
Now the Hourglass
could be anyone...


01:09:48.814 --> 01:09:50.839
a guest of honor...


01:09:50.883 --> 01:09:52.783
maybe even
a stagehand.


01:09:58.224 --> 01:10:01.318
This may be nothing,
but I did see a man


01:10:01.360 --> 01:10:04.022
with what looked like
a canister of


01:10:04.063 --> 01:10:05.394
cerillium.


01:10:05.431 --> 01:10:07.023
Who?


01:10:07.066 --> 01:10:09.534
- This year's lifetime achievement award...
- Him.


01:10:09.568 --> 01:10:12.298
...goes to one of the world's
greatest souls,


01:10:12.338 --> 01:10:15.136
His Holiness,
the Dalai Lama.


01:10:21.781 --> 01:10:24.648
This man isn't who you think
he is, he's the Hourglass.


01:10:24.684 --> 01:10:26.811
No no,
I'm a man of peace.


01:10:26.852 --> 01:10:29.650
Shut up! You're plotting
to kill all these people


01:10:29.689 --> 01:10:31.520
and I can prove it.
Show the world


01:10:31.557 --> 01:10:34.287
the armor you're hiding
under these robes.


01:10:35.461 --> 01:10:36.985
You can't fool me,
Hourglass.


01:10:37.029 --> 01:10:39.657
You're packing 10 lbs
of Cerillium under there.


01:10:39.699 --> 01:10:40.757
- What?
- Ahh!


01:10:44.437 --> 01:10:46.166
Take him down.


01:10:50.443 --> 01:10:52.536
Tutu.


01:10:57.183 --> 01:10:58.582
Peace!


01:10:58.617 --> 01:10:59.982
Pea...


01:11:09.829 --> 01:11:12.127
Shit shit shit shit shit.


01:11:16.335 --> 01:11:18.701
You!


01:11:18.738 --> 01:11:20.467
You're the Hourglass.


01:11:22.742 --> 01:11:25.176
It's a pity you saw that,
my dear.


01:11:25.211 --> 01:11:30.012
Perhaps this will help
you forget.


01:11:35.921 --> 01:11:37.616
What are you doing?


01:11:39.859 --> 01:11:42.020
Take me.


01:12:00.212 --> 01:12:02.009
Hourglass!


01:12:09.221 --> 01:12:12.054
- Hero con?
- It's a convention for people


01:12:12.091 --> 01:12:14.924
who like to dress up
as their favorite heroes and villains.


01:12:14.960 --> 01:12:17.588
- By the way, your costume sucks.
- Out of my way!


01:12:19.432 --> 01:12:21.900
Excuse me,
there is a line.


01:12:23.335 --> 01:12:25.530
No, you're killing him
all wrong.


01:12:25.571 --> 01:12:28.540
It's like this.


01:12:28.574 --> 01:12:31.441
Better.


01:12:33.045 --> 01:12:34.137
Oh, shit.


01:12:49.929 --> 01:12:52.420
Hourglass, you'll never
get away with this!


01:12:52.465 --> 01:12:55.901
Forget it, Dragonfly.
You're too late.


01:12:57.837 --> 01:12:59.805
Run!


01:13:03.108 --> 01:13:04.439
Yeah.


01:13:15.287 --> 01:13:17.414
Goodbye...


01:13:18.891 --> 01:13:19.915
little fly.


01:13:22.495 --> 01:13:24.463
Dragonfly!


01:13:25.498 --> 01:13:27.966
- No!
- Ahhh!


01:13:46.752 --> 01:13:48.947
My eye!


01:13:50.523 --> 01:13:54.118
So, are you gonna
keep the body, or...


01:14:02.334 --> 01:14:03.733
Eh.


01:14:03.769 --> 01:14:08.103
Dragonfly, you must
stop the Hourglass.


01:14:09.875 --> 01:14:11.843
I can't.


01:14:11.877 --> 01:14:13.845
I can't fly.


01:14:13.879 --> 01:14:16.575
If there is one lesson
my life can teach,


01:14:16.615 --> 01:14:20.107
it is that the spirit
is stronger than the body.


01:14:20.152 --> 01:14:22.382
The hero comes from within.


01:14:22.421 --> 01:14:24.514
Those are
Celine Dion lyrics.


01:14:24.557 --> 01:14:27.583
Whatever.
It's still true.


01:14:28.827 --> 01:14:30.158
You're right.


01:14:37.336 --> 01:14:39.327
It's working.


01:14:40.973 --> 01:14:42.873
Sorry.


01:14:43.876 --> 01:14:45.366
Watch, Dragonfly,


01:14:45.411 --> 01:14:47.641
as your city dies.


01:14:59.491 --> 01:15:01.686
Where... am I?


01:15:01.727 --> 01:15:03.957
You're with me,


01:15:03.996 --> 01:15:06.430
your lover.


01:15:12.037 --> 01:15:13.470
Dragonfly!


01:15:15.608 --> 01:15:17.098
No.


01:15:19.278 --> 01:15:22.975
- No.
- Only now do you understand.


01:15:24.249 --> 01:15:27.116
Oh, come...


01:15:28.420 --> 01:15:29.853
Aha!


01:15:31.190 --> 01:15:33.090
I need you to jerk this off.


01:15:35.260 --> 01:15:36.693
Yeah.


01:15:36.729 --> 01:15:38.196
There's not enough time.


01:15:40.933 --> 01:15:42.628
Oh fuck.


01:15:49.675 --> 01:15:52.803
- It's over.
- Dragonfly!


01:15:52.845 --> 01:15:54.836
Jill!


01:15:57.182 --> 01:15:59.047
Gotcha.


01:16:00.786 --> 01:16:03.016
- Rick?
- You didn't think I'd let anything happen


01:16:03.055 --> 01:16:04.955
to the girl I love, did you?


01:16:04.990 --> 01:16:06.685
Well, we're still
falling.


01:16:06.725 --> 01:16:09.922
Damn it!
If only I could fly.


01:16:09.962 --> 01:16:11.987
Maybe I wasn't cut out
to be a hero.


01:16:12.031 --> 01:16:15.023
You know, maybe I was meant
to have a normal job... an accountant,


01:16:15.067 --> 01:16:16.364
a gym teacher.


01:16:16.402 --> 01:16:19.337
- This is a really tall building.
- Rick!


01:16:19.371 --> 01:16:21.339
I don't care
what happens anymore.


01:16:21.373 --> 01:16:23.273
If I die, I die happily
in your arms.


01:16:23.308 --> 01:16:26.573
You're my hero, Rick Riker,
and I love you.


01:16:32.051 --> 01:16:34.952
Yes!
Oh, thank God!


01:16:34.987 --> 01:16:36.887
We only have
50 stories left.


01:16:36.922 --> 01:16:38.719
Hang on.


01:16:49.401 --> 01:16:52.029
Thank you, Dragonfly.


01:16:52.071 --> 01:16:54.869
Because of you, our city
is safe at last.


01:16:54.907 --> 01:16:58.138
- You said it, Dr. Hawking.
- Shit!


01:16:58.177 --> 01:17:00.338
It's a happy ending
